WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.229 --> 00:00:07.560
Let's see. Let's talk to our caller from the
8 6 0 area code who's calling today from 8

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:12.259
6 0 0.
Hi, David. Can you hear me? Yes, I can. Who's

00:00:12.259 --> 00:00:18.279
this?
This is Chris calling from Savannah, Georgia.

00:00:18.279 --> 00:00:24.279
And my question is, last week, Trump's approval
rating kind of skyrocketed. Yeah, it's over

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:30.270
55 percent, I believe. Do you think that this
will really hold? I know that like during

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:35.630
crises, the president's approval rating kind
of goes up because people kind of rally behind

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:39.730
him. But since, you know, coronaviruses is
just the first thing that we have to worry

00:00:39.730 --> 00:00:44.579
about on the recession and stuff, do you see
it necessarily holding and how will that affect

00:00:44.579 --> 00:00:49.539
the election, do you believe?
So a couple of things. Number one, yes. Trump's

00:00:49.539 --> 00:00:55.149
approval rating is up and his handling his
marks, as he likes to call them on coronavirus

00:00:55.149 --> 00:01:00.370
are also pretty high. And so part of it is
that people tend to rally around the president

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:04.089
in a crisis, even if they're doing a pretty
bad job, as I believe Donald Trump is. I think

00:01:04.089 --> 00:01:08.470
the other aspect of this, as you're talking
about, is that not everybody is yet feeling,

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:12.860
you know, when you think about 40 percent
or 35 percent of the cases are in New York,

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:17.980
lots. Large swaths of the country still have
very few cases that they know about.

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:23.460
There are probably a lot of people who are
saying, hey, things are OK here. Trump's doing

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.970
a good job. And of course, that is a lot of
people who simply aren't aware of the real

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:32.500
case. No, because we're not fully testing
yet. However, you bring up a good point, which

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:40.360
is as the unemployment numbers go up and as
this extends, if indeed it does, you may see

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:44.850
that level off or go the other way. But my
prediction, if you say to me, David, you've

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:50.990
got a bet right now, Corona virus helps or
hurts Trump in November. I bet that it helps

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:55.501
even if he continues to handle it poorly,
because there's plausible deniability. There's

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:59.950
always the idea that he could have handled
it worse and things would have been even worse

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:04.500
than they are. And so I if you say, David,
you've got to place a bet. Does this help

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:09.239
or hurt Trump in November? I believe coronavirus
helps Trump in November.

00:02:09.239 --> 00:02:17.400
OK. Yeah. I guess that kind of makes sense.
I think that Trump's been doing.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:23.890
Not not really the best job. No, trying to.
I'm back from college and my parents are like

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:27.700
getting mad at all those journalists and reporters
thinking that they're asking dumb questions

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:32.159
and stuff. And I just kind of get to put my
head down because the pile on me. But it's

00:02:32.159 --> 00:02:41.980
just I don't know. I I kind of will begrudgingly
vote for Biden, I guess, over Trump. But I

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:46.230
I'm just trying to get the word out to people
because I mean, Georgia's kind of going purple.

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:49.920
Yep. We'll see what happens.
We will. We will. And it will really come

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:54.810
down to who who chooses to get out to vote
and how bad will the situation be. You know

00:02:54.810 --> 00:03:00.749
what? What we would unfortunately, if the
Republicans are more likely to believe that

00:03:00.749 --> 00:03:05.300
they shouldn't be staying home, we could end
up with the unfortunate situations that Republican

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:09.530
turnout is significantly higher than Democratic
turnout because Democrats are much more likely

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:12.950
to be staying at home. We don't know what
things will be like in November. You know,

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:16.400
it's eight months away, what, seven, seven
months away? We'll wait and see.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.560
Yeah, that's right, sure. Well, thank you
for taking my question, David, a big fan of

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:25.609
the show and yes, stay safe.
Thank you. Likewise. And I appreciate you

00:03:25.609 --> 00:03:26.569
calling in today.

